      "end": 336.87,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "So, we can have either"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 336.88,
      "end": 338.95,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "a complete case. If we had a matrix that"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 338.96,
      "end": 340.91,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "was diagonal, we would have basically a"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 340.92,
      "end": 343.27,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "star, but that's not the case because if"
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 343.28,
      "end": 345.67,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "we pick, for example, the value C equals"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 345.68,
      "end": 348.63,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "to 1, that puts us on the parabola, we"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 348.64,
      "end": 350.15,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "can see that the matrix AC is not"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 350.16,
      "end": 352.51,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "diagonal, so we are in a defective case."
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 352.52,
      "end": 354.75,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "The defective case,"
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 354.76,
      "end": 356.87,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "if you compute the eigen"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 356.88,
      "end": 359.19,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "values and eigenvector, would give you"
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 359.2,
      "end": 360.47,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "something that looks like that. The"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 360.48,
      "end": 362.87,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "first rate of eigenvector corresponding"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 362.88,
      "end": 366.63,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "to your eigenvalue would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 366.64,
      "end": 368.67,
      "duration": 2.03,
      "text": "in the direction of 1 0. We have"
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 368.68,
      "end": 370.75,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "negative eigenvalues, so it's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 370.76,
      "end": 373.07,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "0. And basically in to determine the"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 373.08,
      "end": 374.75,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "direction, you have to see that we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 374.76,
      "end": 376.91,
      "duration": 2.15,
      "text": "also following a transition here on the"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 376.92,
      "end": 379.39,
      "duration": 2.47,
      "text": "determinant on the on the trace"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 379.4,
      "end": 381.99,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "determinant diagram, and so basically we"
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 382.0,
      "end": 383.47,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "will have"
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 383.48,
      "end": 386.55,
      "duration": 3.07,
      "text": "a spiral that would look like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 386.56,
      "end": 389.71,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "Um yep."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 391.19,
      "end": 391.2,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "What am I doing here? Am I doing the"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 391.2,
      "end": 392.43,
      "duration": 1.23,
      "text": "same thing?"
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 392.44,
      "end": 403.99,
      "duration": 11.55,
      "text": "Yeah."
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 406.87,
      "end": 406.88,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And it would basically rotate"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 406.88,
      "end": 410.11,
      "duration": 3.23,
      "text": "as you can see here"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 415.15,
      "end": 415.16,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 415.16,
      "end": 416.03,
      "duration": 0.87,
      "text": "as"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 416.04,
      "end": 417.87,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "the case that we had just before because"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 417.88,
      "end": 419.67,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "we basically have the transition of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 419.68,
      "end": 422.27,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "structure of the critical point. Okay?"
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 422.28,
      "end": 424.83,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "And we arrows are pointing toward the"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 424.84,
      "end": 426.51,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "critical point again because our two"
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 426.52,
      "end": 429.27,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "eigenvalues are"
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 429.28,
      "end": 431.35,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "are basically here negative. What should"
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 431.36,
      "end": 432.75,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "just repeated eigenvalue that is"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 432.76,
      "end": 433.71,
      "duration": 0.95,
      "text": "negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 433.72,
      "end": 435.71,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "Okay, so now we can move on to a third"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 435.72,
      "end": 439.03,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "case where here we move into the wedge"
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 439.04,
      "end": 441.39,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "area where we have the two eigenvalues"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 441.4,
      "end": 445.03,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "now being real, and both of them are"
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 445.04,
      "end": 447.39,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 447.4,
      "end": 450.59,
      "duration": 3.19,
      "text": "So, for example,"
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 453.91,
      "end": 453.92,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "we would have two eigenvalues"
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 453.92,
      "end": 456.19,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "that would give us two eigenvectors"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 456.2,
      "end": 457.75,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "that are basically the rays. The"
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 457.76,
      "end": 459.27,
      "duration": 1.51,
      "text": "direction of the trajectories on these"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 459.28,
      "end": 461.19,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "two rays would be toward the critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 461.2,
      "end": 463.55,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "point because we have again negative"
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 463.56,
      "end": 467.07,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "eigenvalues. And the trajectories then"
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 467.08,
      "end": 468.79,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "would be following"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 468.8,
      "end": 473.43,
      "duration": 4.63,
      "text": "the lambda. So, if I, for example, pick"
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 473.44,
      "end": 475.39,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "lambda one less than"
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 475.4,
      "end": 477.91,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "lambda two,"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 477.92,
      "end": 480.51,
      "duration": 2.59,
      "text": "then I would have something like this"
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 480.52,
      "end": 484.95,
      "duration": 4.43,
      "text": "going to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 486.75,
      "end": 486.76,
      "duration": 0.01,
      "text": "And we would have this trajectory"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 486.76,
      "end": 488.83,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "corresponding"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 488.84,
      "end": 490.67,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "to the eigenvalue that is the closer to"
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 490.68,
      "end": 492.87,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "0."
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 492.88,
      "end": 493.91,
      "duration": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay?"
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 493.92,
      "end": 495.47,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "And again, the arrows would be going"
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 495.48,
      "end": 497.71,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "toward this critical point. So, we can"
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 497.72,
      "end": 499.67,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "now move on."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 499.68,
      "end": 502.19,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "And if we keep increasing C,"
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 502.2,
      "end": 505.83,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "uh we reach now the point four where we"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 505.84,
      "end": 507.79,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "are in a special case again, a boundary"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 507.8,
      "end": 510.31,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "case where the determinant is 0, but the"
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 510.32,
      "end": 512.07,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "trace is nonzero. If the determinant is"
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 512.08,
      "end": 513.589,
      "duration": 1.509,
      "text": "0, which is the product of the two"
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 513.599,
      "end": 515.23,
      "duration": 1.631,
      "text": "eigenvalues, it means that we have one"
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 515.24,
      "end": 516.79,
      "duration": 1.55,
      "text": "eigenvalue that is"
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 516.8,
      "end": 519.029,
      "duration": 2.229,
      "text": "equal to 0"
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 519.039,
      "end": 521.51,
      "duration": 2.471,
      "text": "and another eigenvalue"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 521.52,
      "end": 523.709,
      "duration": 2.189,
      "text": "that is actually in this case -2, so"
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 523.719,
      "end": 524.95,
      "duration": 1.231,
      "text": "just negative."
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 524.96,
      "end": 527.19,
      "duration": 2.23,
      "text": "So, what happens here? What happens is"
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 527.2,
      "end": 529.59,
      "duration": 2.39,
      "text": "that we have now"
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 529.6,
      "end": 531.51,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "the eigenvector that corresponds to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 531.52,
      "end": 534.27,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "eigenvalue equals to 0 is basically just"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 534.28,
      "end": 537.75,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "defining a whole line of critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 537.76,
      "end": 539.75,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "points. So, all the points on this line"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 539.76,
      "end": 541.23,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "that would correspond, so for example,"
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 541.24,
      "end": 543.43,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "to lambda 0, are all critical points."
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 543.44,
      "end": 544.75,
      "duration": 1.31,
      "text": "So, we don't need to actually draw"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 544.76,
      "end": 546.67,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "arrows here. All the points would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 546.68,
      "end": 548.95,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "critical points. And another direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 548.96,
      "end": 550.63,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "or ray would be determined by the second"
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 550.64,
      "end": 554.11,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "eigenvalue lambda two, and we would"
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 554.12,
      "end": 556.83,
      "duration": 2.71,
      "text": "have, for example,"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 556.84,
      "end": 558.63,
      "duration": 1.79,
      "text": "directions"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 558.64,
      "end": 560.63,
      "duration": 1.99,
      "text": "in this way where it would correspond to"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 560.64,
      "end": 562.23,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "direction of V2. So, all these would be"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 562.24,
      "end": 564.35,
